      "shareMode": "customScheduled",
      "status": "sent",
      "text": "From the McKinseys; article what resonated  with me is the paradigm shift in seeing AI as acoworker. This fundamentally shifts the human role from being an isolated executor of tasks to an orchestrator of intelligent systems. The future of work is a direct partnership between people, software agents, and physical robots.\ufffc\ufffc\n\nThis reminds me of the dynamic between a master chef and a team of highly skilled sous-chefs; the sous-chefs (agents) handle the repetitive chopping and prep work, allowing the master chef (the human) to focus entirely on the final seasoning, taste-testing, and presentation. \n\nThe same In software product development, developers act as orchestrators by using coding agents to rapidly draft boilerplate code and run automated tests. This allows the human product engineers to redirect their focus toward high-level system architecture, complex debugging, and defining the overall product strategy.\ufffc https://www.mckinsey.com/mgi/our-research/agents-robots-and-us-skill-partnerships-in-the-age-of-ai?cid=eml-web",
